{"name":"Spooky Graveyard","hex":"#685e4f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spooky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Eerie, or suggestive of ghosts or the supernatural.","Spooked; afraid; frightened."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spooky"},{"term":"graveyard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tract of land in which the dead are buried.","A final storage place for collections of things that are no longer useful or useable.\n\n The discard pile, in some trading card games.\n\n A team where players are sent when they are not useful, or a team where players become useless if sent there."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graveyard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cemetery","blocks":[{"text":"A cemetery, burial ground, gravesite, graveyard, or a green space called a memorial park or memorial garden, is a place where the remains of many dead people are buried or otherwise entombed. The word cemetery implies that the land is specifically designated as a burial ground and originally applied to the Roman catacombs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Kerepesi_temet%C5%91_Budapest.jpg/330px-Kerepesi_temet%C5%91_Budapest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cemetery"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Cemetery_in_China.jpg/500px-Cemetery_in_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Cemetery_in_China.jpg/1280px-Cemetery_in_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Cemetery_in_China.jpg/500px-Cemetery_in_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cemetery in China","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F